From 8a7b4f5900834a2f767f1c75cdf4993aae5a6ad4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:08:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] buildroot: target ISA rv64gc - a rootfs every riscv64
 runs

The CVITEK musl cross-gcc defaults to rv64gc + T-Head extras (v0p7,
zfh, xtheadc); every target binary was silently tagged for a C906-with-
thead core, so the rootfs ran on CVITEK silicon only - qemu-system-
riscv64 -M virt (plain RV64GC) took an illegal instruction in /init.
The prebuilt musl libc itself is clean rv64gc and the toolchain ships
the matching ld-musl-riscv64.so.1, so pinning the compile flags is all
it takes:

  BR2_TARGET_OPTIMIZATION="-march=rv64gc -mabi=lp64d"

Same package set, same scripts; C906 boards lose nothing but unused
T-Head ISA tags and gain an image that boots under QEMU and any future
riscv64 board - which is the point of the universal family image.
Kernel configs are untouched (per-board, and the C906 thead features
there are selected by the vendor Kconfig, not by this flag).
---
 buildroot/configs/cvitek_SG200X_musl_riscv64_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/buildroot/configs/cvitek_SG200X_musl_riscv64_defconfig b/buildroot/configs/cvitek_SG200X_musl_riscv64_defconfig
index 7634161a1..e59b1b6d9 100644
--- a/buildroot/configs/cvitek_SG200X_musl_riscv64_defconfig
+++ b/buildroot/configs/cvitek_SG200X_musl_riscv64_defconfig
@@ -215,7 +215,7 @@ BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_UCONTEXT=y
 BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_OPENMP=y
 BR2_TOOLCHAIN_SUPPORTS_PIE=y
 BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTRA_LIBS=""
-BR2_TARGET_OPTIMIZATION=""
+BR2_TARGET_OPTIMIZATION="-march=rv64gc -mabi=lp64d"
 BR2_TARGET_LDFLAGS="-mcpu=c906fdv -march=rv64imafdcv0p7xthead -mcmodel=medany -mabi=lp64d"
 BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HEADERS_AT_LEAST_3_0=y
 BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HEADERS_AT_LEAST_3_1=y
